  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/2d08bcbbcd7ec4d8c388d24728c3f3afdc7c954497f342e9ac2b459fad24e5d2.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\u222c}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{x}^{2}}3\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[y]_{y=1}^{y=2-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[2-{x}^{2}-1]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[3x-{x}^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(3-1)-(-3+1) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
